WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:04.380
Disturbing things had been happening on the
fifth floor of the Rose Heights apartment

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:07.190
building in Albany, New York.

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:11.519
Residents had reported strange noises over
the last few days.

00:00:11.519 --> 00:00:15.480
Screaming in the night, pained muttering,
soft weeping.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.679
Scratching and scuttling in the walls.

00:00:17.679 --> 00:00:24.529
And worst of all, what seemed like an infestation
of bugs unlike anything the unfortunate occupants

00:00:24.529 --> 00:00:27.029
of Rose Heights had ever seen before.

00:00:27.029 --> 00:00:33.250
They weren’t abnormal in size or shape - they
looked an awful lot like the common earwig,

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:37.899
around two and a half centimeters long with
large, curved pincers on the back.

00:00:37.899 --> 00:00:44.310
But the color wasn’t right - unlike the
usual dark brown, these earwigs were a silvery,

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.620
almost translucent gray.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:51.059
When people spotted them crawling across their
walls or hiding in the carpet, they seemed

00:00:51.059 --> 00:00:52.769
to shimmer in the light.

00:00:52.769 --> 00:00:56.930
Eventually the building’s landlady, Donna
Tompkins, was called in to do something about

00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:58.339
the infestation.

00:00:58.339 --> 00:01:03.809
She spoke to each of the residents about their
experience - they reported the strange noises,

00:01:03.809 --> 00:01:08.200
the mysterious bugs, and even a funny smell
they’d sometimes catch in the hall.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:11.270
A smell like someone had thrown up.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:15.650
And every single person that Donna spoke to
couldn’t help but remark that the smell

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:21.940
was particularly strong outside the apartment
of a certain resident, Bill Parham.

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:26.520
Stranger still was the fact that Bill hadn’t
been seen in days.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:30.140
Donna knocked on his door, but received no
answer.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:35.240
She called him on his cell phone and could
hear the phone ringing inside the apartment,

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:37.490
but it just went to voicemail.

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:41.370
When she checked the security footage of the
lobby, she saw that Bill hadn’t left the

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:44.050
building in the last few days either.

00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:49.800
Donna called the police, worried that Bill
might be sick or even dead inside his apartment.

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:53.860
It was strange, given that he was only in
his thirties and didn’t seem to have any

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:57.970
health conditions, but stranger things had
happened.

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:01.250
Much stranger things were about to happen,
too.

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:03.990
Two police officers arrived not long after.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:08.530
They called through the door one more time,
and when they got no response, Donna gave

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:10.729
them the key to head inside.

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:12.340
The apartment was a wreck.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:14.860
All the furniture was covered in dust.

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:18.460
Filthy dishes were piled high in the sink
and on the draining board.

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:20.880
The smell of rot was thick in the air.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:25.860
There were empty boxes of painkillers, all
the pills popped from their silvery foil,

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.250
laying on the ground.

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.960
But worst of all were the bugs.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:34.640
The apartment was crawling with them, and
they were on every surface.

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:36.940
Those silvery gray earwigs.

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:42.000
Neither of the officers liked bugs, and it
seemed that the deeper they got into the apartment,

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.140
the more bugs there were.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:48.540
Some even seemed to be crawling towards them
- pointing their pincers at them as though

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:51.260
they were defending their territory.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:56.090
This looked to be a textbook case of what
happens when a resident keels over and dies,

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:58.330
but there was just one problem.

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:00.200
Where was the body?

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:05.360
Bill Parham had seemingly dropped off the
face of the earth, and now, a colony of mysterious

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:09.360
bugs had started squatting in his apartment
in his absence.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.620
Then came that smell again.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:15.710
That truly awful smell, like bile and blood.

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:21.320
It was even stronger now and it seemed like
it was coming from a nearby closet.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:25.440
The two officers, acting on pure instinct,
drew their weapons and approached the closet

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:26.790
with caution.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:30.570
Even if they weren’t consciously aware of
it, they knew they were going to find something

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:32.650
awful inside.

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:34.640
Something evil.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.540
Something dangerous.

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:40.160
When they threw open the closet door, they
couldn’t help but scream.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:41.920
They’d found the nest.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:47.459
It was a huge, round hive, like the biggest
beehive you’ve ever seen, melded to the

00:03:47.459 --> 00:03:49.550
lower corner of the closet.

00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:54.770
The unnatural earwigs were crawling into,
out of, and around it.

00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:55.870
Thousands of them.

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:57.940
Tens of thousands of them.

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:02.560
And the second they registered the presence
of the two officers, intruders into their

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:05.380
nest, they began to swarm.

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:09.760
In sheer panic, both raised their guns and
opened fire into the closet, but it didn’t

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:11.310
do them any good.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:15.750
Their bullets just pierced and splintered
the hive, causing even more enraged insects

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:19.059
to spill out and begin crawling over the two
cops.

00:04:19.059 --> 00:04:23.330
They fled from the apartment, screaming in
pain from the gnashing pincers of the insects

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:25.289
crawling all over their skin.

00:04:25.289 --> 00:04:27.889
They never did find the corpse of Bill Parham.

00:04:27.889 --> 00:04:31.000
But that’s because Bill Parham wasn’t
dead.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:35.539
At least, not until mere moments ago, when
the bullets from the cops’ guns had torn

00:04:35.539 --> 00:04:37.710
through his bones and perforated his organs.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:43.160
He died not long after, and if he could still
speak close to the end, he would have thanked

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:45.180
them both for the mercy.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:48.610
Because the monstrosity that they’d just
encountered in the closet wasn’t just a

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:51.939
nest of mysterious insects in Bill Parham’s
apartment.

00:04:51.939 --> 00:04:54.759
It was Bill himself.

00:04:54.759 --> 00:04:59.610
This is the fate worse than death in store
for anyone supremely unlucky enough to fall

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:07.180
victim to SCP-439, better known by the nickname
for their unique nests, The Bone Hive.

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:11.210
And while these nasty little critters may
be small, they’re filled with enough pure

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:16.169
nightmare fuel to send you running into 682’s
containment chamber for a little comfort.

00:05:16.169 --> 00:05:21.570
Let’s go through the whole nightmarish process,
and tell you exactly what happened to poor

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:23.189
Bill Parham.

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:28.719
First discovered by the SCP Foundation in
mainland China, SCP-439 specimens largely

00:05:28.719 --> 00:05:31.749
get by on the fact they’re not much to look
at.

00:05:31.749 --> 00:05:35.589
Unless you’re an entomologist, when you
see a strange insect, you probably just accept

00:05:35.589 --> 00:05:39.870
the fact it’s a perfectly normal breed you’ve
just never encountered before.

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:43.879
Nobody is hammering down the doors of their
local news station to alert the press about

00:05:43.879 --> 00:05:48.320
the gray earwig they saw crawling out of a
crack in their bathroom wall.

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:52.629
But if Bill Parham had done just that, it
would have saved his life.

00:05:52.629 --> 00:05:58.009
The Foundation would have immediately flagged
the incident as an SCP-439 infestation, and

00:05:58.009 --> 00:06:00.830
dispatched a mobile task force to deal with
it.

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:05.180
Instead, when Bill saw the earwig for the
first time, he was getting ready for work

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:07.719
and didn’t have the time to stop and deal
with it.

00:06:07.719 --> 00:06:12.380
He made a mental note to buy some bug killer
on the way home, but quickly forgot.

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:14.400
The insect didn’t forget him, though.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:19.939
In fact, it thought he would be a perfect
candidate for the SCP-439 process.

00:06:19.939 --> 00:06:24.779
The Foundation has tested extensively with
the one SCP-439 sample they’ve been able

00:06:24.779 --> 00:06:27.069
to successfully catch and contain.

00:06:27.069 --> 00:06:32.719
In all these tests, they found that 439 specimens
rejected hosts from any species other than

00:06:32.719 --> 00:06:33.719
humans.

00:06:33.719 --> 00:06:36.360
They’re an extraordinarily specific parasite.

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:43.150
It’s also only one particular type of SCP-439
specimen that you actually need to worry about:

00:06:43.150 --> 00:06:44.779
The Queens.

00:06:44.779 --> 00:06:51.439
Despite their superficial similarities, SCP-439
behave nothing like non-anomalous earwigs.

00:06:51.439 --> 00:06:56.349
Normal earwigs are not social creatures, they’re
solitary scavengers and they don’t keep

00:06:56.349 --> 00:06:58.659
nests as permanent habitats.

00:06:58.659 --> 00:07:02.689
The same can definitely not be said for SCP-439.

00:07:02.689 --> 00:07:08.779
They have complex social structures, much
like that of bees, ants, and termites, with

00:07:08.779 --> 00:07:11.999
queens, scouts, workers, and warriors.

00:07:11.999 --> 00:07:16.680
If you happen to encounter a worker or warrior,
you may get a painful pinch from their pincers

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:18.379
if you get too close.

00:07:18.379 --> 00:07:23.130
But if you end up on the wrong side of one
of the queens, then you have a much, much

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:25.529
worse fate in store for you.

00:07:25.529 --> 00:07:30.900
And it just so happened that the SCP-439 specimen
that appeared in Bill Parham’s bathroom

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:33.410
that morning was visiting royalty.

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:39.520
This 439 queen had selected her target, and
now, it was time to move to the next part

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:43.339
of the process: Initial infiltration.

00:07:43.339 --> 00:07:47.400
When Bill returned home from work, he was
delighted to find that the gray earwig was

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:51.240
nowhere to be seen - but that didn’t mean
it was gone.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:55.960
It was still there, lurking, it just didn’t
want to be seen.

00:07:55.960 --> 00:08:00.119
After all, the real fun would happen after
Bill went to bed.

00:08:00.119 --> 00:08:05.419
Once SCP-439 detects that its potential host
has fallen into a deep sleep, it will crawl

00:08:05.419 --> 00:08:10.710
onto the person’s body, and into their mouth,
which is exactly what it did to Bill.

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:14.889
It feels like little more than a tickle in
your throat, and you will have no idea that

00:08:14.889 --> 00:08:19.439
the tiny creature crawling down your windpipe
and into the soft, warm tissue of your lungs

00:08:19.439 --> 00:08:21.490
spells your doom.

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:24.099
Very few people wake up during this process.

00:08:24.099 --> 00:08:28.379
But even if they did, there’s virtually
nothing they could do.

00:08:28.379 --> 00:08:33.320
When Bill woke up, he was suffering from mild
chest pains and shortness of breath, a symptom

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:36.310
not uncommon in a number of respiratory ailments.

00:08:36.310 --> 00:08:41.630
He had no idea that the SCP-439 Queen was
already inside him.

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:45.850
He got up and went about his day, trying to
ignore the pain as it gradually grew worse

00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:51.089
and worse, feeling almost like something was
moving inside his chest.

00:08:51.089 --> 00:08:56.089
He spent the whole day having to stop to let
out a deep, hacking cough, but coughing didn’t

00:08:56.089 --> 00:08:57.839
expel or change anything.

00:08:57.839 --> 00:09:02.940
He looked and felt so terrible that his boss
let him go home early, hoping that Bill would

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:06.500
be able to sleep off whatever illness he thought
he had picked up.

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:10.680
But over the next couple days, his condition
only worsened.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:15.730
The pain grew so excruciating he could barely
move, and he was popping painkillers like

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:17.920
tic tacs, to no effect.

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:22.850
He started running a dangerously high fever,
his body trying in vain to fight back against

00:09:22.850 --> 00:09:24.600
its lethal intruder.

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:30.250
He felt worse than he ever had in his life,
but little did poor Bill know, the most terrible

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:33.190
parts of the process were yet to come.

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:39.410
Through anomalous means, an SCP-439 infection
is able to induce Fibrodysplasia ossificans

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:44.970
progressiva, or FOP, in its victims, which
is typically a genetic disease that presents

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:48.209
itself before the victim turns ten years old.

00:09:48.209 --> 00:09:53.100
The condition is infamous for its primary
symptom: Turning muscle and other soft tissue

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:59.230
into bone, slowly but surely paralyzing the
victim and putting them in a state of unspeakable

00:09:59.230 --> 00:10:00.230
pain.

00:10:00.230 --> 00:10:05.029
This bone transformation process is known
as “Ossification”, and Bill was about

00:10:05.029 --> 00:10:07.380
to experience it first hand.

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:12.360
His pain increased as his mobility decreased,
with more of his flesh becoming solid lumps

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:14.940
of bone underneath the skin.

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:18.019
Soon enough, all he knew was pain.

00:10:18.019 --> 00:10:23.600
It’d become so agonizing that he was delirious
with it, he was drunk on pain.

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:26.829
Even perceiving sunlight felt like being stabbed
in the eyes.

00:10:26.829 --> 00:10:32.329
That’s why, like all the other victims of
SCP-439, he decided to conceal himself in

00:10:32.329 --> 00:10:35.399
a warm, dark place where no light could get
to him.

00:10:35.399 --> 00:10:39.029
In Bill’s case, of course, that place was
his closet.

00:10:39.029 --> 00:10:43.580
He was hurting so bad that all he could do
was curl up into the fetal position and weep

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:48.120
as his muscles turned to bone and his body
began to compact and shrink.

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:53.480
He didn’t even look like a human anymore
- he was more like a ball, covered in a bone

00:10:53.480 --> 00:10:56.290
shell and filled with warm organs.

00:10:56.290 --> 00:11:01.029
That’s when the queen started laying eggs
among his organs.

00:11:01.029 --> 00:11:06.990
It wasn’t long before there was a new brood
of around 30,000 specimens living inside Bill’s

00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:07.990
body.

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:13.300
He was still very much alive, but there wasn't
anything he could do about his situation.

00:11:13.300 --> 00:11:18.790
His muscles had long since turned to bone,
and they had eaten large portions of his brain,

00:11:18.790 --> 00:11:23.069
leaving mainly the parts needed to keep his
organs just barely functioning.

00:11:23.069 --> 00:11:27.130
After all, the colony still needs central
heating.

00:11:27.130 --> 00:11:32.000
SCP-439 colonies have developed a perfect
parasitic relationship with the human body.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:37.149
They even use the stomach inside the hive
to predigest food into a liquid slurry that’s

00:11:37.149 --> 00:11:39.019
easier for them to consume.

00:11:39.019 --> 00:11:43.800
The only loser in this situation is someone
like Bill, who is forced to become the new

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:47.160
home for the world’s most nightmarish freeloaders.

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:51.980
Eventually, when the colony becomes too big,
a queen departs to start a new one, and the

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:54.550
process repeats itself once more.

00:11:54.550 --> 00:11:59.329
It’s enough to make you want to sleep with
your mouth closed for the rest of your life.

00:11:59.329 --> 00:12:02.580
Oh, and we haven’t even told you the worst
part yet.

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:08.149
Foundation scientists have conducted tests
on some victims of SCP-439, and found that

00:12:08.149 --> 00:12:12.690
while the creatures do consume large parts
of the brain, the parts they leave are capable

00:12:12.690 --> 00:12:13.930
of consciousness.

00:12:13.930 --> 00:12:20.360
That’s right, their victims remain aware
of what’s happening to them the whole time,

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:23.629
even when they hardly seem human at all anymore.

00:12:23.629 --> 00:12:28.439
What actually finally kills the victims of
SCP-439 isn’t the bodily trauma.

00:12:28.439 --> 00:12:33.009
It’s the starvation that sets in when the
colony inevitably moves on.

00:12:33.009 --> 00:12:34.709
Did we just hear you cough?

00:12:34.709 --> 00:12:36.640
You might want to go get that checked out…

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:43.030
Now go watch “SCP-001 - When Day Breaks”
and “SCP-823 - Carnival of Horrors” for

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:45.820
more terrifying SCPs that’ll chill you to
the bone!

